## HLS Protocol Overview

Lament uses **HTTP Live Streaming (HLS)** for audio playback. Rather than downloading monolithic audio files, tracks are split into index playlist files (`.m3u8`) and sequential 10-second audio segment files (`.ts`).

---

## Edge Hotlink Protection Architecture

To prevent unauthorized external hotlinking of raw audio files stored on Cloudflare R2:

1. **Edge WAF Referer Rule**: Cloudflare WAF validates the `http.referer` header on all `/hls/` audio requests to ensure traffic originates from authorized client domains (`lament.rynds.my.id` or `localhost`).
2. **Server Proxy Routing**: SvelteKit server routes proxy playlist requests (`/api/stream/:id/playlist.m3u8`), attaching client API keys server-side so credentials remain hidden from client browsers.

---

## Client Integration (`HLS.js`)

In the SvelteKit frontend client, `HLS.js` manages segment fetching and buffer strategy:

```typescript
import Hls from 'hls.js';

if (Hls.isSupported()) {
  const hls = new Hls({
    enableWorker: true,
    lowLatencyMode: true,
    xhrSetup: (xhr) => {
      xhr.setRequestHeader('x-api-key', clientApiKey);
    }
  });

  hls.loadSource('/api/stream/trk_7f9a2b1c/playlist.m3u8');
  hls.attachMedia(audioElement);
}
```
